<td tEditID="c1r2" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; color:#000000; bEditID:r3st1; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r2" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[Hi&nbsp;<span class="ui-provider fy b c d e f g h i j k l m n o p q r s t u v w x y z ab ac ae af ag ah ai aj ak" dir="ltr" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 102);">[Insert Name]</span>&nbsp;,<div><br></div><div>Thank you again for all that you did to support the Red Cross hospital patients by hosting a blood drive.&nbsp; Your blood drive helped make a lasting difference for hospital patients and their loved ones. I hope you will continue to be involved in our lifesaving mission as you move forward in your life.</div><div><br></div><div>Now that your blood drive is complete, the last step is to find a student who will take over your Red Cross leadership position.&nbsp; Transitioning your Blood Program Leader role means that patients will receive ongoing support and local blood needs can be met during critical collection periods.&nbsp; It will also help ensure your blood drive moves forward and grows year after year, even after you graduate, becoming part of your school's legacy.</div><div><br></div><div>I'd like for you to think of an outstanding student leader to take over your blood drive.&nbsp; Now is the best time to find a new student to take over while the blood drive is fresh on everyone's mind.</div><div><br></div><div>Once you find a student who is interested, please pass along their contact information to me so that I can introduce myself.&nbsp; Thank you for your help with this important last step.&nbsp; Let me know if you have any questions and I look forward to hearing back from you.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks again,</div><div><span class="ui-provider fy b c d e f g h i j k l m n o p q r s t u v w x y z ab ac ae af ag ah ai aj ak" dir="ltr" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 102);">[Insert Name]</span></div><div>&nbsp;</div>]]></td>
</tr>
